nGHS hazard pictogram: black exclamation mark inside a red diamond outline.\n</visual_element>\n\nSignal Word: Warning\n\nHazard Statements:\n- Causes skin irritation.\n- Causes serious eye irritation.\n\nPrecautionary Statements:\n\n**Prevention:**\n- Wash skin thoroughly after handling.\n- Wear protective gloves/ eye protection/ face protection.\n\n**Response:**\n- IF ON SKIN: Wash with plenty of water.\n- IF IN EYES: Rinse cautiously with water for several minutes. Remove contact lenses, if present and easy to do. Continue rinsing.\n- If skin irritation occurs: Get medical advice/ attention.\n- If eye irritation persists: Get medical advice/ attention.\n- Take off contaminated clothing and wash it before reuse.\n\n**Other hazards which do not result in classification**  \nNone known.\n\n## 3. COMPOSITION/INFORMATION ON INGREDIENTS\n\nSubstance / Mixture: Substance\n\n**Components**\n\n<table id=\"e2\">\n\n| Chemical name | CAS RN | Concentration (% w/w) | ENCS/ISHL number |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sodium Nicotinate | 54-86-4 | >= 98 - <= 100 | ENCS 5-6624<br>ISHL 8-(1)-679 |\n\n</table>\n\n1 / 7--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ngifter reference atlas · 2026.39.1 (https://alberdilab.github.io/gifter/atlas/)\nciteturn34search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; 76  | NAMN  | NAMN  | unspecified  | nicotinate D-ribonucleotide  | CHEBI:57502  | Nicotinate mononucleotide: the junction where de novo quinolinate chemistry, nicotinate salvage and cobamide lower-ligand attachment all meet.  | nicotinate D-ribonucleotide(2-)\n| D-erythrose 4-phosphate(2-)\n72  | PLP  | PLP  | unspecified  | pyridoxal 5'-phosphate  | CHEBI:597326  | Vitamin B6 in its catalytically active form, which is also the product of both biosynthetic routes, so no separate activation step exists to exclude.  | pyridoxal 5'-phosphate(2-)\n73  | PIMELOYL_COA  | PIMELOYL_COA  | cytoplasmic  | pimeloyl-CoA  | CHEBI:57360  | Cytoplasmic seven-carbon dicarboxylic thioester that supplies the biotin valeric acid side chain. The marker layer does not distinguish it from the acyl-carrier-protein thioester used by the BioC/BioH route, so the anchor names the CoA form and the claim covers both; both carriers are intracellular in the curated routes.  | pimeloyl-CoA(5-)\n74  | BIOTIN  | BIOTIN  | unspecified  | biotin  | CHEBI:57586  | Vitamin B7, the carboxyl carrier cofactor of acetyl-CoA and pyruvate carboxylases.  | biotinate\n75  | QUINOLINATE  | QUINOLINATE  | unspecified  | quinolinate  | CHEBI:29959  | Committed pyridine precursor of NAD, and the point at which de novo synthesis is separated from salvage.  | quinolinate(2-)\n76  | NAMN  | NAMN  | unspecified  | nicotinate D-ribonucleotide  | CHEBI:57502  | Nicotinate mononucleotide: the junction where de novo quinolinate chemistry, nicotinate salvage and cobamide lower-ligand attachment all meet.  | nicotinate D-ribonucleotide(2-)\n77  | NAD  | NAD  | unspecified  | NAD(+)  | CHEBI:57540  | Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide, the product that makes a genome independent of exogenous niacin.  | NAD(1-)\n78  | NICOTINATE  | NICOTINATE  | unspecified  | nicotinate  | CHEBI:32544  | Vitamin B3 as acquired from the environment; the input boundary of pyridine salvage.  | nicotinate\n79  | UROGEN_III  | UROGEN_III  | unspecified  | uroporphyrinogen III  | CHEBI:57308  | Tetrapyrrole branchpoint. Heme, siroheme and the corrin ring all leave shared metabolism here, which is why the cobalamin claim starts at this molecule and not earlier.  | uroporphyrinogen III(8-)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPRACE N A UKOWE INSTYTUTU OCHRONY ROSLIN (https://agro.icm.edu.pl/agro/element/bwmeta1.element.agro-5118116f-3f2a-470d-b071-ac62d1f5be83/c/Prace_Nauk_Insty_Ochro_Ros_r.1960_t.II_nr.2_s.15-34.PDF)\nciteturn34search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; wolm:, od wirusa bez termicznego traktowania, a tylko przez dwukrotne ... o handlowej nazwie „Cytovirin\".\nrusa rośliny ziemniaka przez rozmnażanie etiolowanych pędów szczyto-\nwych, przy czym oddziaływanie temperaturami 30, 35 lub 38°C w cią­\ngu 23 dni nie było co prawda konieczne, ale ułatwiało osiągnięcie tego \nwyniku. \nMe 1 che r s (1958) \nwyraził na IV \nMiędzynarodowym Kongresie \nOchrony Roślin pogląd, w myśl którego wypracowanie jakiegoś wiri-\ncydu zasadniczo nie należy do rzeczy beznadziejnych. Tymczasem uka-\nzały się doniesienia Gr a y a (1957a i b) oraz Luc as a i W i n st e a-\nd a (1958), według których w badawczych laboratoriach Mercka, Sharpa \ni Dohmea w Rahway w stanie N ew Jersey został opracowany viricyd \no handlowej nazwie „Cytovirin\". Jest to krystaliczny antybiotyk wy-\ntwarzany przez pewien gatunek Streptomyces. Preparat ten spowodo-\nwał w doświadczeniach G r a y a kompletne zahamowanie tworzenia się \nu fasoli ogrodowej lokalnych ognisk porażenia wywoływanych w na-\nstępstwie sztucznego zakażenia południowym wirusem moza,iki tytoniu. \nTo samo zostało stwierdzone w przypadku wirusa mozaiki tytoniu na--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALFAAB22224 (https://assets.thermofisher.com/DirectWebViewer/private/document.aspx?prd=ALFAAB22224~~PDF~~MTR~~CGV4~~EN~~2026-01-03+05%3A27%3A48~~Sodium+nicotinate~~)\nciteturn34search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; ## Sodium nicotinate ... | ACGIH | American Conference of Governmental Industrial Hygienists | IARC | International Agency for Research on Cancer | ... | RPE | Respiratory Protective Equipment | LD50 | Lethal Dose 50% |\nALFAAB22224\n\n# SAFETY DATA SHEET\n## Sodium nicotinate\n\nPage 7 / 8  \nRevision Date 02-Jan-2026\n\n---\n\n## International Inventories\n\nX = listed, China (IECSC), Europe (EINECS/ELINCS/NLP), U.S.A. (TSCA), Canada (DSL/NDSL), Philippines (PICCS), Japan (ENCS), Japan (ISHL), Australia (AICS), Korea (KECL).\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n\n| Component | The Inventory of Hazar